Subject: [PATCH v7 9/9] jails/instances/lab-mail: Sync the whole account into
 INBOX
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: rqvvtqsnzoxqpqppunwpspvxrwplpvvk
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:30:10 +0000

Each post waits in a Dovecot INBOX that sits outside the maildir and
outside the sync, so it reaches neither Fastmail nor the readers of
lists until Pat moves it by hand. Mail that Fastmail holds outside
lists and Archive never reaches lab-mail either. The account is the
list's own and holds no other mail, so there is nothing to sort or
keep from readers: the whole account is the list.

- mbsync syncs every folder, and creates on lab-mail a folder that is
  new on Fastmail.
- INBOX is a folder of the maildir, so a post reaches Fastmail and
  every reader on the next sync.
- Dovecot no longer creates lists, and nothing files mail into it.
  The spec drops the Fastmail rule, and posts and the jj maildir
  import land in INBOX.
- Readers may read every folder. mbsync may also create one.
